Third-party material
--------------------

integration/croc/user_pkg.sv.example and integration/croc/user_domain.sv.example
reproduce scaffolding from pulp-platform/croc (ETH Zurich and University of
Bologna), which is licensed under the Solderpad Hardware License, Version 0.51.
Those two files are provided as diff references for an integrator; only the
CORDIC-specific parts of them are covered by this repository's licence.

integration/croc/lint/obi_pkg.sv and integration/croc/lint/croc_pkg.sv reproduce
the type and configuration field lists from pulp-platform/obi and
pulp-platform/croc, same licence, so that the integration wrapper can be
elaborated for linting without a Croc checkout. They are for linting only and
must never be compiled into a Croc build.

The CORDIC algorithm itself is due to Jack Volder (1959) for the circular case
and John Walther (1971) for the unified circular, linear and hyperbolic form,
including the repeated-iteration rule for hyperbolic convergence. Both are
published prior art, not code.

No source code from any other project is included in rtl/, tb/, sw/ or scripts/.
